#  What the image is allowed to see.
#
#  An allowlist rather than a list of things to leave out, because the
#  expensive mistake here is the one you forget: .env sits in this directory
#  with a database password in it, and a build context is uploaded to a
#  builder machine whether or not any COPY line ever reads it. Starting from
#  "nothing" means a new file is excluded until somebody says otherwise.
#
#  Keep this in step with infra/Dockerfile. If a COPY there fails with "file
#  not found" and the file plainly exists, it is excluded here.

*
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!packages
!apps
!infra
!testdata

# Caches and build output, which are large, machine-specific, and would
# invalidate a layer on every build.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.venv
**/dist
**/*.egg-info

# Tests and fixtures do not ship in the image. The e2e suite in particular
# pulls Playwright in, which has no business in a runtime image.
**/tests
